Subject: [PATCH] stamp-p4: do not record a crash capsule on a requested reboot

The restart handler arms the MWDT for 1 ms.  With 0054 stage 0 is the
pretimeout interrupt, so every normal `reboot` wrote a WDT CRASH_CAPSULE
that looked like a real hang (#19).  Claim the capsule before arming so
the pretimeout ISR leaves it alone; panic/die paths claim it earlier and
still win.

---
diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/esp32p4_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/esp32p4_wdt.c
--- a/drivers/watchdog/esp32p4_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/esp32p4_wdt.c
@@ -484,6 +484,9 @@
 {
 	struct esp32p4_wdt *wdt = watchdog_get_drvdata(wdd);
 
+	/* A requested reboot is not a crash: no capsule for this arm. */
+	atomic_set(&crash_claimed, 1);
+
 	esp32p4_wdt_arm(wdt, 1);	/* fire in 1 ms */
 	mdelay(100);			/* reset happens under us */
 
